# MCAT Speedrun — Core Rules

## Product scope

- MCAT exam (472–528). Prototype on **~15–25 topics**, not a full prep course.
- Fork Anki + AnkiDroid; **shared Rust engine**. No parallel scheduler in other languages.

## Three scores (never blend)

1. **Memory** — FSRS / revlog recall
2. **Performance** — accuracy on curated exam-style MCQs (separate from cards)
3. **Readiness** — mapped range with coverage penalty; abstain if coverage < ~50%

## Two modes

- **Memory mode:** normal Anki reviews
- **Performance mode:** separate session; only **topic-gated** content (≥3 cards seen, ≥5 Good/Easy)
- **CARS:** performance-only, no flashcard gate
- Never: flip card → instant performance question

## Question bank

- Curated from **named sources** (OpenStax primary); store `source_name`, `source_url`, `topic_id`, `split`
- Runtime performance mode reads **local bank** — no live LLM during review
- Wednesday deliverable: **no AI**

## Error typing (BrainLift)

On performance miss, support: `content_gap`, `passage_mapping`, `reasoning`, `misread` → drives dashboard next action.

## Honesty (Speedrun — automatic fail if violated)

No readiness without: range, coverage %, confidence, missing-data note, single next action.

## Study feature

Interleaved vs blocked **performance** sessions; 3-build ablation vs plain Anki.

## Docs

Before large changes, align with `docs/PRD.md` and `docs/DECISIONS.md`.
